Interactive USD edits of lights and cameras, with the usd procedural cache_id and with the render delegate

A grey sphere is lit by a distant light whose color and intensity change, then the camera moves away from the
sphere and back, the stage being re-rendered after each edit. The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural reading the
stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session, and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate
driven like a Hydra host, see testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the
last procedural render is compared against the reference image.

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
